{"t":1794364885821,"type":"say","kind":"cannot","why":"The reply says it cannot do the requested task with its tools: it cannot watch the video, and it cannot add new audio to the original footage without changing the picture. It then offers alternatives and asks which one the user wants. The main content is the inability, so \"cannot\" fits better than \"question,\" even though the reply ends by asking for a choice.","called":true,"text":"I tried, but I can't make this one the way you asked. Two things block it:\n\n1. **I can't watch the video.** None of my tools play it back to me. The most I got was a face scan, which found about three people at the start and one later on. I can't see what they're doing, so any narration I wrote \"explaining what's happening\" would be made up.\n2. **I can't put new audio on your footage without changing it.** My tools can generate new video clips, edit or restyle video, translate the speech, or lip-sync a face. None of them can remove the original conversation, lay a voice-over on the same 10 seconds and leave the picture exactly as it is. The narration tool only works on videos it generates itself, not on footage you upload.\n\nNothing was charged. The face scan is free.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **You write or describe it, then you add it.** Tell me in a sentence or two what happens in the clip. I'll write a short, friendly voice-over script timed to 10 seconds, and you can record it or add it in any basic video editor.\n- **A translated version.** If you only want the conversation in another language, I can run the video translator on the full 10 seconds. It keeps the picture and replaces the speech.\n- **A new video.** I can generate a new 10-second narrated clip that recreates the scene, with no music or captions. It would be AI-made footage, though, not your original.\n\nWhich would you like?"}
